    {
        "content": "<p>pchickey requested <a href=\"https://github.com/alexcrichton\">alexcrichton</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15054\">PR #15054</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635844620,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793227911
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15054#pullrequestreview-5704201753\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Some of this is going to be dependent on the PR this is built-on, but my general impression here is that this is a fair bit of special-casing which naively seems like it may not be necessary with some refactoring in other places. Would it be possible to experiment to shift things around to do that? For example how come <code>HelperLocation::Stack</code> can't be used for GC references since it's always a single param and a single result?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636111723,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793304389
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15054#discussion_r4417300378\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In the interest of avoiding special-casing where possible, could this be removed? Similarly below the special-case to skip the get/set on the stack seems like it could be removed too. I'd otherwise expect that a GC reference is basically always represented as \"stack\" since that's basically another name for \"in a local\"</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636111725,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793304390
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>fitzgen <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15054#issuecomment-6507491821\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15054\">PR #15054</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For example how come <code>HelperLocation::Stack</code> can't be used for GC references since it's always a single param and a single result?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>See <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4417440249\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4417440249</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would it be possible to experiment to shift things around to do that?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Sure, I can poke at some more stuff, but if you have any other ideas, let me know...</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636115411,
